<title>USA: Mich. jobless rate inches up in January to 4.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Mich. jobless rate inches up in January to 4.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Michigan's unemployment rate rose slightly to a seasonally adjusted 4.9 percent in January from 4.8 percent in December, the state's employment security agency reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>The number of workers without jobs increased by 8,000 to 240,000 from 232,000 in December. In January 1996, Michigan saw a five percent jobless rate.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, the agency reported that the size of the state's labor force grew by 42,000 to 4.88 million.</p>
<p>((Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647))</p>
